closed_loop_reward.description:
Canonical Closed-Loop AIS Control Zone (`green` / `yellow` / `red` with hysteresis)
and Step/Epoch Reward Evaluation. `r_total` uses the profile named in `reward_profile`;
the default is multiplicative: `max(0, R_task) * AIS / 1000`, zero when gated.

get.description:
Returns all broker counters in one call. Every field is an atomic load —
zero allocation, zero contention. Raw cumulative counters are exposed;
clients compute rates by polling.

RegimeDecisionLabel.description:
Prediction targets: not_eligible = reference selection is not separate-scale;
supported = eligible and separation-test p-value upper bound <= 0.05;
unsupported = eligible and lower bound > 0.05; unresolved = eligible and
lower <= 0.05 < upper. These are offline numerical rank bounds, not served
scores or confidence intervals. Unresolved is never a serving failure.

label.description:
Prediction targets: not_eligible = reference selection is not separate-scale;
supported = eligible and separation-test p-value upper bound <= 0.05;
unsupported = eligible and lower bound > 0.05; unresolved = eligible and
lower <= 0.05 < upper. These are offline numerical rank bounds, not served
scores or confidence intervals. Unresolved is never a serving failure.

RegimeVolatilityPrediction.description:
Rule-selected label: crisis when result.crisis.status is crisis, otherwise
the student's state (LOWER_VOL is low, HIGHER_VOL is high). It has no scores;
score_contract does not apply to it.

tags.description:
Operator-facing endpoints. `/health` returns 503 when the
agent is degraded (dependency down, scheduler paused);
`/metrics` exposes Prometheus text.

password.description:
Minimum **10** characters — not 8; this is 2026. At least one letter and one
digit, checked against a top-1000 common-password list. The 128 cap is for sanity;
BCrypt truncates at 72 bytes regardless.

SearchHit.description:
One result row in a search group. `group` names the owning resource;
`id` is the resource's own id; `kind` is a display hint; `title` is the
primary match text; `subtitle` carries context (ip / run / severity / …);
`payload` carries the fields each group needs to deep-link. Minimal and
presentation-free: the webapp and CLI render from the same fields.

